      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn perfect squares and nearest-square problems with a small example.\n\nWe will build the method one step at a time and check each answer.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A perfect square has every prime factor appearing an even number of times.\n\nExample: 900 = 2²×3²×5².\n\nAll exponents are even, so 900 is a perfect square.\n\nA last digit can give a quick warning, but factor structure is the proof.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
